# velero bootstrap

## 1. Cloud bucket/region — done

`helm/velero/values.yaml` `backupStorageLocation[0]` (name: `cloud`) points
at `loki-homelab-backup` / `ap-south-1`, and the `velero` namespace +
`velero-cloud-credentials` Secret (key `cloud`, AWS-credentials-file blob)
already exist in-cluster — reused the access key from an older host-cron
tar+gpg+S3 backup job, created directly via `kubectl` (never written to a
file that outlived the command, never committed). Nothing left to do here
unless that key is rotated.

## 2. Create the local credential Secret (never committed)

Velero's AWS plugin expects the credential Secret to hold one key (`cloud`)
whose value is a full AWS-credentials-file blob, `[default]` profile.

Local (backup-minio — same MINIO_ROOT_USER/PASSWORD set up in
`helm/backup-minio/.setup`):

```
cat > /tmp/velero-local-creds <<'EOF'
[default]
aws_access_key_id=<MINIO_ROOT_USER>
aws_secret_access_key=<MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD>
EOF
kubectl -n velero create secret generic velero-local-credentials \
  --from-file=cloud=/tmp/velero-local-creds
shred -u /tmp/velero-local-creds
```

## 3. Install the velero CLI (for manual backup/restore commands)

```
# https://velero.io/docs/latest/basic-install/#install-the-cli
```

## The four jobs

**Cloud backup — automatic.** The `cloud-weekly` Schedule in values.yaml
runs `0 3 */7 * *` (every 7 days, 03:00) against the `cloud` BSL, `includedNamespaces: ["*"]`
(so every `homelab-*` PVC-backed namespace), 30-day TTL. Trigger one
out-of-band the same way:

```
velero backup create cloud-manual-$(date +%Y%m%d) --storage-location cloud
```

**Cloud restore — manual, always.**

```
velero backup get                                    # find the backup name
velero restore create --from-backup <backup-name>
```

**Local (hard-drive) backup — manual only, no Schedule.**

```
velero backup create local-$(date +%Y%m%d) --storage-location local
```

**Local restore — manual.**

```
velero backup get --storage-location local
velero restore create --from-backup <backup-name>
```

## Scope note

`arr`'s media/torrents tree (`homelab-arr`) is a hostPath mount, not a PVC
(see `helm/arr/values.yaml` comment on it) — Velero's fs-backup only
captures PVC-backed pod volumes, so it's excluded automatically. No
per-namespace exclusion needed.
